# Agent state. Almost all of it is machine-local churn — regenerable caches,
# per-turn logs, chat exports (which also carry session tokens) — so it stays out
# of git. The durable, hand-written parts are re-included below.
#
# Four lines, in this order, and each one matters:
#   `.cptr`     is load-bearing. cptr's auto-gitignore check
#               (cptr/utils/workspace.py) looks for that exact line and appends
#               one when absent — at the END of the file, where (last match wins)
#               it would override every `!` below and silently void the allowlist.
#   `!.cptr/`   re-includes the directory itself; git will not descend into an
#               excluded directory, so without this the `!` lines can never apply.
#   `.cptr/*`   excludes the contents — same coverage as a bare `.cptr`, but
#               without excluding the parent, which is what makes `!` possible.
.cptr
!.cptr/
.cptr/*
!.cptr/skills/
!.cptr/artifacts/
*.log

# Local runtime artifacts (server launched from this checkout)
cptr-pid.txt
downloads/
notes/_scratch/
